    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "farthest corner of a forest, the night, delightful on account",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "of the expanse of the sky being brightened up by the winter",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "moonshine, solely intent on storing up merit.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "7. Our view ( at first ) was that you were we and we",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "were you (i. e. you and we were the same, had no diverging",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "interests); what has happened now by which you are you",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "and we are we ( i. e. you and we have had diverging",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "interests ) ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "8. What if one has a threadbare wallet or a spotless",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "white silken cloth ? What if one has only one's wife, or is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "surrounded by a splendid army of horses and elephants ?",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "What if delicious food is eaten, or coarse food towards the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "close of the day ? What if there is not the light ( of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "knowledge of Brahman ) manifested inside ( i. e. in the heart",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "or what if there is the glorification in which the fear of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "worldly existence is destroyed ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "9. When there was ignorance ( in us ) produced by the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "influence of the darkness of passion, even the whole world",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "was then looked upon (by us) as consisting of women only;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "now having applied the collyrium of better judgment, our",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "sight has been restored to its normal state and regards the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "whole world as Brahman.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "10. Knowledge in the case of the good does away with",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "conceit vanity and the like; in the case of others ( lit. some )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "it is the cause of haughtiness and vanity. A secluded place",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "in the case of self-restraining persons leads to salvation; in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "the case of love-sick persons it is a further incitement to love.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "11. I consider those men to be supremely rich, who have",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "never joined their palms overhead in token of submission, to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "whom a slab on some mountain is as a couch and a cave in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "mountain as a home, to whom the barks of trees are as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "raiment and the deer as friends, whose subsistence is by the",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
